n the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/alabama/monroe-county"],["ARC or PLC in Monroe County","/arc-plc/alabama/monroe-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 13 grids September to October came in under 90% of normal in 36 of them. In 2025 that same pair ran 46% of normal on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, May to June came in at 221% of normal there. Grid 13672 had its driest year in 1954 at 53% of normal.</p>"}
